WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.086 --> 00:00:04.058
Bob Cratchit reached for Tiny Tim's hand.

2
00:00:04.059 --> 00:00:10.379
He squeezed it, looking at the frail little boy with deep love in his eyes.

3
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:15.182
"Cratchit adores that child," Scrooge said.

4
00:00:15.183 --> 00:00:19.629
"Spirit . . ." He paused to look at the ghost.

5
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:25.828
"You must tell me, will Tiny Tim live to see another Christmas?"

6
00:00:25.829 --> 00:00:33.223
"I'm afraid I see a vacant seat at next year's table," the spirit said solemnly.

7
00:00:33.224 --> 00:00:40.569
"I see a tiny crutch leaning against the empty chair."

8
00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:43.486
He turned to look at Scrooge.

9
00:00:43.487 --> 00:00:52.834
"If nothing happens to change the course of the future, the child will die before another Christmas arrives."

10
00:00:52.835 --> 00:01:00.919
"No, no." Scrooge found himself filled with sadness at this terrible news.

11
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:07.965
He looked again at Tiny Tim's little hand, still clasped in his father's loving grip.

12
00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:15.416
"Oh no, kind spirit. Please tell me the boy will be spared!"

13
00:01:15.417 --> 00:01:20.979
"I'm surprised to hear such a request from you," the spirit said.

14
00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:27.678
"Your only concern with this child before tonight was how much it must cost to support him.

15
00:01:27.679 --> 00:01:34.251
You even hoped that his father didn't use him as an excuse to ask you for a raise."

16
00:01:34.252 --> 00:01:43.359
Scrooge's face twisted with guilt. "I didn't mean it," he muttered. "I was just . . ."

17
00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:46.766
At that moment he heard his own name.

18
00:01:46.767 --> 00:01:50.596
Bob Cratchit had raised a glass for a toast.

19
00:01:50.597 --> 00:01:55.949
"To Mr. Scrooge, the provider of this feast!"

20
00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.939
His wife scowled. "The provider of this feast?

21
00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:06.362
I won't drink to the health of a cold, stingy man like Mr. Scrooge."

22
00:02:06.363 --> 00:02:13.587
"My dear," Bob Cratchit said mildly, "it's Christmas."

23
00:02:13.588 --> 00:02:18.859
"Then I'll drink to his health for your sake and for the season," she said.

24
00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:23.259
"Not for Mr. Scrooge, who's the ogre of this family.

25
00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:26.674
He pays you as little as he can get away with."

26
00:02:26.675 --> 00:02:31.965
"Merry Christmas and Happy New Year to Mr. Scrooge," Tiny Tim said.

27
00:02:31.966 --> 00:02:36.957
"Everyone deserves a blessing at Christmastime!"

28
00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:43.420
Even his mother couldn't disagree with that, and so the family drank the toast.

29
00:02:43.421 --> 00:02:48.255
"I'm grateful they're thinking of me," Scrooge muttered.

30
00:02:48.256 --> 00:02:52.861
"But blessings and toasts have little value in the real world.

31
00:02:52.862 --> 00:02:57.835
Cratchit should spend more time on figuring out how to help his sick child.

32
00:02:57.836 --> 00:03:01.674
It's a desperate situation."

33
00:03:01.675 --> 00:03:05.444
Suddenly the house and the family disappeared.

34
00:03:05.445 --> 00:03:09.051
Scrooge stood once more on a city street.

35
00:03:09.052 --> 00:03:16.596
It was dark, and snow was falling, but the warm glow of fires lightened the gloom around them.

36
00:03:16.597 --> 00:03:24.064
Scrooge and the spirit began walking along, peeking through one window after another.

37
00:03:24.065 --> 00:03:30.692
They saw a family preparing for a cozy dinner with plates warming over the fire.

38
00:03:30.693 --> 00:03:37.821
A plump, smiling woman closed the curtains to shut out the cold and darkness.

39
00:03:37.822 --> 00:03:42.554
In another house the blinds were closed tightly.

40
00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:49.439
But Scrooge could see the shadows of people inside, dancing and laughing.

41
00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:57.161
Then several lovely teenage girls came out of a house, wearing fur boots and warm, hooded coats.

42
00:03:57.162 --> 00:04:05.016
Chattering happily, they hurried next door to invite their neighbor to join their family for dinner.

43
00:04:05.017 --> 00:04:09.826
Scrooge listened as the man accepted their invitation.

44
00:04:09.827 --> 00:04:14.419
"His face is glowing with joy," Scrooge thought.

45
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:19.884
He was just about to point out the man to the spirit when a church bell rang.

46
00:04:19.885 --> 00:04:25.047
To Scrooge's surprise, the Ghost of Christmas Present disappeared.

47
00:04:25.048 --> 00:04:28.370
So did everything else around him.

48
00:04:28.371 --> 00:04:34.795
Scrooge heard a sound and turned to see a different phantom moving toward him.

49
00:04:34.796 --> 00:04:39.772
It was tall and covered in a black garment with a hood.

50
00:04:39.773 --> 00:04:47.619
Scrooge couldn't see its face, its body, or anything else except one thin, outstretched hand.

51
00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:52.221
Its mysterious presence filled Scrooge with a terrible dread.

52
00:04:52.222 --> 00:05:01.174
"Am I . . . Are you the Ghost of Christmas Future?" Scrooge asked in a shaky voice.

53
00:05:01.175 --> 00:05:09.659
The spirit said nothing. It only lifted its hand, pointing a finger past Scrooge.

54
00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:16.390
"You're about to show me the shadows of things that will happen in the future," Scrooge said.

55
00:05:16.391 --> 00:05:19.306
"Is that true, spirit?"

56
00:05:19.307 --> 00:05:24.757
The spirit tilted its head but still said nothing.

57
00:05:24.758 --> 00:05:29.305
By now Scrooge was almost accustomed to his ghostly visitors.

58
00:05:29.306 --> 00:05:36.436
Even so, he felt so afraid of this new spirit that his whole body trembled.

59
00:05:36.437 --> 00:05:39.849
"Ghost of the Future!" he cried.

60
00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:43.729
"I'm more afraid of you than the other ghosts.

61
00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.099
But I know your purpose is to do me good.

62
00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.403
I am prepared to follow where you will lead.

63
00:05:50.404 --> 00:05:53.980
But why won't you speak to me?"

64
00:05:53.981 --> 00:05:58.155
The finger pointed again.

65
00:05:58.156 --> 00:06:13.361
Then the mysterious spirit began drifting in that same direction, and Scrooge followed it wearily.

